1
00:00:01,543 --> 00:00:03,504
HEY, I JUST GOT MY, UH...
TEACHER EVALUATIONS.

2
00:00:03,545 --> 00:00:05,965
CHECK OUT WHAT
THIS ONE STUDENT WROTE.

3
00:00:06,005 --> 00:00:09,384
"I LOVED DR. GELLER'S CLASS.
MIND-BLOWING LECTURES.

4
00:00:09,426 --> 00:00:11,595
"DR. GELLER, YOU ARE DEFINITELY

5
00:00:11,637 --> 00:00:14,807
THE 'HOTTIE'
OF THE PALEONTOLOGY DEPARTMENT."

6
00:00:17,058 --> 00:00:19,353
AH, "HOTTIES OF THE PALEONTOLOGY
DEPARTMENT."

7
00:00:19,394 --> 00:00:21,438
THERE'S A BIG SELLING CALENDAR,
HUH?

8
00:00:22,648 --> 00:00:23,899
WHO WROTE IT?

9
00:00:23,941 --> 00:00:25,275
OH, I WISH I KNEW

10
00:00:25,317 --> 00:00:26,735
BUT THE EVALUATIONS
ARE ALL ANONYMOUS.

11
00:00:26,777 --> 00:00:28,195
DO YOU STILL HAVE
THEIR FINAL EXAMS?

12
00:00:28,236 --> 00:00:29,196
YEAH.

13
00:00:29,237 --> 00:00:30,489
OH. 'CAUSE YOU COULD JUST MATCH

14
00:00:30,531 --> 00:00:31,824
THE EVALUATION TO THE EXAM

15
00:00:31,866 --> 00:00:33,492
WITH THE SAME HANDWRITING
AND, BOOM

16
00:00:33,534 --> 00:00:34,869
THERE'S YOUR ADMIRER.

17
00:00:34,910 --> 00:00:36,119
A HOT GIRL'S AT STAKE

18
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:38,163
AND ALL OF A SUDDEN,
HE'S RAIN MAN.

19
00:00:39,748 --> 00:00:41,667
HEY, WAIT A MINUTE,
WAIT A MINUTE.

20
00:00:41,709 --> 00:00:43,919
WHY ARE WE SO SURE
THAT THIS IS A GIRL?

21
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:49,550
IT'S A GIRL.

22
00:00:50,759 --> 00:00:52,344
ANYWAY, IT WOULDN'T MATTER,
OKAY?

23
00:00:52,386 --> 00:00:54,262
BECAUSE I'M A TEACHER,
SHE'S A STUDENT.

24
00:00:54,304 --> 00:00:55,764
OH, IS THAT AGAINST
THE RULES?

25
00:00:55,806 --> 00:00:57,641
NO, BUT IT IS FROWNED UPON.

26
00:00:57,683 --> 00:00:59,018
I SEE.

27
00:00:59,059 --> 00:01:00,268
BESIDES, THERE'S
A BIG AGE DIFFERENCE.

28
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:01,687
WELL, THINK OF IT
LIKE THIS

29
00:01:01,729 --> 00:01:02,938
WHEN YOU'RE 90...

30
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:04,398
I KNOW. WHEN I'M 90,
SHE'LL BE, LIKE, 80

31
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:06,400
AND IT WON'T SEEM LIKE SUCH
A BIG DIFFERENCE.

32
00:01:06,441 --> 00:01:10,362
NO, THAT'S NOT WHAT I WAS
GOING TO SAY AT ALL.

33
00:01:10,404 --> 00:01:11,947
NO. WHAT I WAS
GOING

34
00:01:11,989 --> 00:01:14,449
TO SAY IS WHEN
YOU'RE 90 YOU'LL
STILL HAVE THE MEMORY

35
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:15,826
OF WHAT IT WAS
LIKE TO BE

36
00:01:15,868 --> 00:01:16,952
WITH A 20-YEAR-OLD.

37
00:01:24,001 --> 00:01:29,214
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

38
00:01:29,256 --> 00:01:31,466
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

39
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:33,802
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

40
00:01:33,844 --> 00:01:38,766
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

41
00:01:38,807 --> 00:01:41,268
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

42
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:44,438
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

43
00:01:44,479 --> 00:01:47,733
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

44
00:01:47,775 --> 00:01:53,697
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

45
00:01:57,826 --> 00:01:59,578
HEY, CHANDLER,
YOU KNOW THAT GIRL

46
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:02,497
YOU WENT TO COLLEGE WITH
WHO BECAME A MOVIE DIRECTOR?

47
00:02:02,539 --> 00:02:03,874
OH, YEAH, DANA KEYSTONE.

48
00:02:03,916 --> 00:02:05,542
SHE WAS IN MY MOVEMENT CLASS.

49
00:02:05,584 --> 00:02:07,795
WHAT'S A MOVEMENT CLASS?

50
00:02:07,836 --> 00:02:10,005
IT'S CHANDLER'S WAY
OF PRETENDING

51
00:02:10,047 --> 00:02:11,381
HE DIDN'T TAKE MIME.

52
00:02:11,423 --> 00:02:14,175
WELL, LISTEN, ANYWAY,
SHE'S DIRECTING

53
00:02:14,217 --> 00:02:15,677
THE NEW AL PACINO MOVIE.

54
00:02:15,719 --> 00:02:17,012
YOU GOT TO GET ME AN AUDITION.

55
00:02:17,054 --> 00:02:19,264
I HAVEN'T TALKED
TO HER IN TEN YEARS.

56
00:02:19,306 --> 00:02:21,349
OH, NO, NO, NO.
PLEASE, PLEASE, CHANDLER?

57
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:22,392
I WOULD OWE YOU SO MUCH.

58
00:02:22,434 --> 00:02:24,185
YOU DO OWE ME SO MUCH.

59
00:02:24,227 --> 00:02:25,813
YOU OWE ME $3,400...

60
00:02:25,854 --> 00:02:28,857
DUDE, WHY ARE YOU
CHANGING THE SUBJECT?

61
00:02:28,899 --> 00:02:31,276
WILL YOU MAKE
THE CALL OR WHAT?

62
00:02:31,318 --> 00:02:32,527
OKAY, I'LL TRY.
ALL RIGHT.

63
00:02:32,569 --> 00:02:33,654
THANKS.
YOU'RE THE BEST.

64
00:02:33,695 --> 00:02:34,989
NOW, LISTEN

65
00:02:35,030 --> 00:02:36,573
THE LAST DAY OF AUDITIONS IS
THURSDAY, OKAY?

66
00:02:36,615 --> 00:02:38,533
SO I GOT TO GET IN THERE
BY THURSDAY, OKAY?

67
00:02:38,575 --> 00:02:39,994
JUST REMEMBER THURSDAY.
THURSDAY.

68
00:02:40,035 --> 00:02:41,202
CAN YOU REMEMBER THURSDAY?

69
00:02:41,244 --> 00:02:43,580
YEAH, SO, TUESDAY?

70
00:02:45,165 --> 00:02:46,291
THURSDAY.

71
00:02:46,333 --> 00:02:48,043
LOOK, IF YOU NEED
HELP REMEMBERING

72
00:02:48,085 --> 00:02:49,336
JUST THINK OF IT
LIKE THIS:

73
00:02:49,377 --> 00:02:51,379
THE THIRD DAY, ALL RIGHT?

74
00:02:51,421 --> 00:02:52,547
MONDAY, ONE DAY.

75
00:02:52,589 --> 00:02:54,466
TUESDAY, TWO DAY.

76
00:02:54,508 --> 00:02:56,802
WEDNESDAY, WHEN? HUH?
WHAT DAY?

77
00:02:56,844 --> 00:02:58,137
THURSDAY!

78
00:02:58,177 --> 00:03:01,180
THE THIRD DAY, OKAY?

79
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:02,975
THANK YOU.

80
00:03:03,017 --> 00:03:03,934
OKAY. GOOD.

81
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:07,521
HEY, MON, I'M GOING
TO CHECK MY MESSAGES.

82
00:03:07,562 --> 00:03:09,188
YOU JUST THOUGHT
OF THAT IN THERE?

83
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:10,732
SURE. YOU KNOW,
NATURE CALLED.

84
00:03:10,774 --> 00:03:12,359
SHE WANTED TO SEE
WHO ELSE DID.

85
00:03:13,568 --> 00:03:16,947
HELLO?

86
00:03:16,989 --> 00:03:18,365
UH, RACHEL.

87
00:03:18,406 --> 00:03:20,034
YOU GUYS, SOMEONE IS
IN OUR APARTMENT.

88
00:03:20,075 --> 00:03:21,869
CALL THE COPS!

89
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:24,412
YOU'RE ON THE PHONE!

90
00:03:24,454 --> 00:03:25,873
OH, MY GOD!

91
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:27,206
WHAT?

92
00:03:27,248 --> 00:03:28,249
OH, MY GOD. THANK YOU.

93
00:03:28,291 --> 00:03:29,793
THAT WAS THE FIRE DEPARTMENT.

94
00:03:29,835 --> 00:03:31,294
THERE WAS A FIRE AT OUR PLACE!

95
00:03:31,336 --> 00:03:32,337
OH, MY GOD!

96
00:03:32,379 --> 00:03:33,714
HOW BAD WAS IT?

97
00:03:33,755 --> 00:03:35,966
WELL, HE DIDN'T SAY,
BUT IT WAS A FIRE.

98
00:03:36,008 --> 00:03:37,384
I'M GUESSING
NOT VERY GOOD.

99
00:03:37,425 --> 00:03:38,510
COME ON.
WE GOT TO GO.

100
00:03:38,552 --> 00:03:39,720
YEAH, COME ON.

101
00:03:39,761 --> 00:03:42,597
WHAT ARE YOU
SMILING ABOUT?

102
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:44,058
WHAT IS SO FUNNY?

103
00:03:44,099 --> 00:03:46,768
THE PART I WANT
TO AUDITION FOR
IS A FIREMAN.

104
00:03:46,810 --> 00:03:48,478
THIS IS SO MEANT TO BE!

105
00:03:56,486 --> 00:03:57,571
WOW!

106
00:03:57,612 --> 00:03:58,947
LOOKS LIKE YOU WERE
VERY GENEROUS

107
00:03:58,989 --> 00:04:00,407
WITH YOUR GRADES
THIS SEMESTER.

108
00:04:00,448 --> 00:04:01,783
( chuckles )

109
00:04:06,997 --> 00:04:07,998
PROFESSOR GELLER?

110
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:09,041
YEAH?

111
00:04:09,083 --> 00:04:10,125
I WANTED TO SAY

112
00:04:10,167 --> 00:04:12,293
HOW MUCH I ENJOYED
YOUR CLASS.

113
00:04:12,335 --> 00:04:13,294
OH, THANK YOU.

114
00:04:13,336 --> 00:04:14,379
THANKS VERY MUCH.

115
00:04:14,421 --> 00:04:16,464
OW.

116
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:17,966
UM, I'M A LITTLE EMBARRASSED

117
00:04:18,008 --> 00:04:20,260
ABOUT CALLING YOU
A HOTTIE ON MY
EVALUATION.

118
00:04:20,301 --> 00:04:21,595
THAT WAS YOU?

119
00:04:21,636 --> 00:04:22,596
YEAH.

120
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:24,556
I FELT A LITTLE WEIRD ABOUT IT.

121
00:04:24,598 --> 00:04:25,557
YOU'RE A TEACHER.

122
00:04:25,599 --> 00:04:26,600
I'M A STUDENT

123
00:04:26,641 --> 00:04:27,976
BUT WOULD YOU

124
00:04:28,018 --> 00:04:29,937
MAYBE WANT TO GO OUT
WITH ME SOMETIME?

125
00:04:29,978 --> 00:04:33,941
OH, I DON'T THINK THAT WOULD BE
THE BEST IDEA.

126
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:37,444
OH, 'CAUSE I WAS THINKING...
THE SEMESTER IS OVER.

127
00:04:37,485 --> 00:04:39,780
YOU'RE NOT MY TEACHER ANYMORE.

128
00:04:39,821 --> 00:04:40,989
WHAT TIME?

129
00:04:43,324 --> 00:04:45,202
OH, YOU KNOW WHAT?
FORGET IT.

130
00:04:45,244 --> 00:04:47,412
I SEE YOU
ALREADY GAVE ME AN "A."

131
00:04:48,997 --> 00:04:49,957
GOTCHA.

132
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:51,959
I'M KIDDING! GOD!

133
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,043
OH.

134
00:04:53,085 --> 00:04:56,255
SO, SERIOUSLY,
WHAT TIME?

135
00:04:59,758 --> 00:05:00,717
Phoebe:
COMING THROUGH.

136
00:05:00,759 --> 00:05:01,718
OH! COMING THROUGH.

137
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:02,677
OH, HELLO.

138
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:03,804
HI.

139
00:05:03,845 --> 00:05:05,180
NO. RIGHT.

140
00:05:05,222 --> 00:05:06,181
COMING THROUGH.

141
00:05:06,223 --> 00:05:07,474
OKAY, WELL,
IT'S NOT SO BAD.

142
00:05:07,515 --> 00:05:08,892
YEAH, MOST OF THE DAMAGE

143
00:05:08,934 --> 00:05:10,978
IS PRETTY MUCH CONTAINED
TO THE BEDROOMS.

144
00:05:11,019 --> 00:05:11,895
OH!

145
00:05:11,937 --> 00:05:13,396
HEY, BUDDY

146
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:15,649
YOU THINK I COULD BORROW
YOUR UNIFORM THIS THURSDAY?

147
00:05:15,690 --> 00:05:17,151
EXCUSE ME?

148
00:05:17,192 --> 00:05:19,402
JOEY, HE'S WORKING.

149
00:05:19,444 --> 00:05:22,072
YOU WOULD LOOK
GOOD IN THAT.

150
00:05:24,032 --> 00:05:25,033
HOW BAD IS IT?

151
00:05:25,075 --> 00:05:27,077
OH, IT'S BAD.
IT'S REALLY BAD.

152
00:05:27,119 --> 00:05:30,371
THE ONLY THING THERE
THAT ISN'T BURNED IS AN AX

153
00:05:30,413 --> 00:05:32,457
WHICH I DO NOT
REMEMBER BUYING.

154
00:05:32,499 --> 00:05:33,708
HOW'S YOUR ROOM, RACH?

155
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:36,170
EVERYTHING'S RUINED:
MY BED, MY CLOTHES.

156
00:05:36,211 --> 00:05:37,754
LOOK AT MY FAVORITE
BLUE SWEATER.

157
00:05:37,796 --> 00:05:38,797
ISN'T THAT MINE?

158
00:05:38,839 --> 00:05:42,383
FINE. I'M SORRY
FOR YOUR LOSS.

159
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:44,094
SO, UH, YOU'RE NOT

160
00:05:44,136 --> 00:05:46,013
GOING TO BE ABLE
TO LIVE HERE FOR A WHILE.

161
00:05:46,054 --> 00:05:47,472
YOU LADIES
HAVE A PLACE TO STAY?

162
00:05:47,514 --> 00:05:51,518
OH, WOW. OKAY.

163
00:05:51,559 --> 00:05:54,938
LOOK, PAL, I AM
NOT IN THE MOOD

164
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:56,190
TO BE HIT ON
RIGHT NOW.

165
00:05:56,231 --> 00:05:57,858
BUT IF YOU GIVE
ME YOUR NUMBER

166
00:05:57,899 --> 00:05:59,734
I WILL CALL YOU
SOME OTHER TIME.

167
00:06:02,654 --> 00:06:04,363
YES. THEY CAN
STAY WITH US.

168
00:06:04,405 --> 00:06:05,490
HAVE YOU FIGURED OUT

169
00:06:05,532 --> 00:06:07,326
WHAT STARTED
THE FIRE, MR. FIREMAN?

170
00:06:07,366 --> 00:06:10,704
WELL, UH, DO EITHER OF YOU
SMOKE?

171
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:12,206
NO, NOT USUALLY

172
00:06:12,247 --> 00:06:14,373
BUT, YEAH, I COULD USE
ONE RIGHT NOW. THANKS.

173
00:06:14,415 --> 00:06:16,668
NO, NO, NO. DO YOU LIGHT
CANDLES, BURN INCENSE?

174
00:06:16,710 --> 00:06:19,046
YES, I DO ALL THE TIME.

175
00:06:19,087 --> 00:06:20,339
I LOVE THEM!

176
00:06:20,379 --> 00:06:21,631
OH, MY GOD. I DID IT.

177
00:06:21,673 --> 00:06:23,217
IT'S ME, IT'S ME.

178
00:06:23,258 --> 00:06:25,677
I BURNED DOWN THE HOUSE!
I BURNED DOWN THE HOUSE!

179
00:06:25,719 --> 00:06:27,721
OKAY, PHOEBE, CALM DOWN.
THERE'S NO NEED

180
00:06:27,762 --> 00:06:29,806
TO PLACE BLAME, OKAY?

181
00:06:29,848 --> 00:06:32,767
I WARNED HER
ABOUT THOSE CANDLES.

182
00:06:35,270 --> 00:06:36,855
GOD, IT'S GREAT
TO CATCH UP.

183
00:06:36,897 --> 00:06:38,899
I CAN'T BELIEVE
HOW LONG IT'S BEEN.

184
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,525
HEY, CHANDLER, IS THAT...?

185
00:06:42,652 --> 00:06:43,904
OH, THAT'S GREAT.

186
00:06:43,945 --> 00:06:45,030
GOOD FOR YOU.

187
00:06:45,072 --> 00:06:46,198
HEY, HEY, HEY,
IS IT...?

188
00:06:47,615 --> 00:06:51,870
OKAY, SO, YEAH, MAYBE
WE CAN GET TOGETHER, UM...

189
00:06:57,876 --> 00:06:59,753
CAN YOU HOLD ON
FOR ONE SECOND, PLEASE?

190
00:06:59,794 --> 00:07:01,420
WHAT?

191
00:07:01,462 --> 00:07:03,798
WHEN YOU'RE OFF THE PHONE,
YOU WANT TO GET A PIZZA?

192
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:06,968
HI, I'M BACK.

193
00:07:07,010 --> 00:07:08,678
YEAH, THAT SOUNDS GREAT.

194
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:10,680
OKAY, WELL, WE'LL DO IT THEN.

195
00:07:10,722 --> 00:07:11,681
OKAY, BYE.

196
00:07:11,723 --> 00:07:14,393
( gasps )

197
00:07:14,433 --> 00:07:15,894
HEY, LISTEN, SO
WHEN'S MY AUDITION?

198
00:07:15,936 --> 00:07:17,104
I MEAN, I KNOW
IT'S THURSDAY

199
00:07:17,145 --> 00:07:18,105
BUT WHAT TIME?

200
00:07:18,146 --> 00:07:19,314
HEY.
HI.

201
00:07:19,356 --> 00:07:21,400
WE DIDN'T GET
TO THE AUDITION.

202
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:24,278
I'LL TAKE HER TO COFFEE
AND THEN WE'LL DO IT THEN.

203
00:07:24,319 --> 00:07:25,612
WOW. SO, NOW YOU'RE GOING

204
00:07:25,653 --> 00:07:27,030
ON A DATE WITH THIS GIRL?

205
00:07:27,072 --> 00:07:28,198
HONEY, IT IS
NOT A DATE.

206
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:29,657
I HAVEN'T TALKED
TO HER IN TEN YEARS.

207
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:30,784
YOU CAN'T CALL UP
SOMEBODY

208
00:07:30,825 --> 00:07:32,286
YOU HAVEN'T TALKED
TO IN TEN YEARS

209
00:07:32,327 --> 00:07:33,453
AND ASK THEM FOR A FAVOR.

210
00:07:33,494 --> 00:07:34,454
THERE ARE RULES.

211
00:07:34,495 --> 00:07:35,830
YOU GOT TO PUT
IN SOME TIME.

212
00:07:35,872 --> 00:07:36,957
YOU'RE RIGHT. I'M SORRY.

213
00:07:36,998 --> 00:07:38,250
IT'S NOT LIKE, YOU KNOW

214
00:07:38,292 --> 00:07:39,793
YOU'RE GOING OUT
WITH AN EX-GIRLFRIEND.

215
00:07:39,834 --> 00:07:40,961
NO, WE ONLY
WENT OUT ONCE.

216
00:07:41,002 --> 00:07:43,046
YOU DATED HER?!

217
00:07:43,088 --> 00:07:45,757
NOT ONCE.

218
00:07:45,799 --> 00:07:49,303
GREAT. WELL, WHY DON'T I JUST GO
OUT WITH AN EX-BOYFRIEND

219
00:07:49,344 --> 00:07:51,305
AND, YOU KNOW, DO JOEY A FAVOR?

220
00:07:51,346 --> 00:07:53,181
HEY, YOU WANT
TO DO JOEY A FAVOR?

221
00:07:53,223 --> 00:07:54,766
MAYBE YOU GO OUT
WITH JOEY.

222
00:07:57,477 --> 00:07:59,520
( gasps )

223
00:08:03,275 --> 00:08:04,443
OH, THAT'S GREAT.

224
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:06,486
MY FRIEND JOEY'S
IN THE MOVIE BUSINESS.

225
00:08:06,527 --> 00:08:08,571
MM, YOU KNOW WHO I RAN
INTO FROM SCHOOL?

226
00:08:08,613 --> 00:08:09,614
HOWIE.

227
00:08:09,656 --> 00:08:13,243
MY FRIEND'S NAME IS JOEY.

228
00:08:13,285 --> 00:08:15,412
APPARENTLY, HOWIE'S EDITING NOW.

229
00:08:15,454 --> 00:08:17,622
YEAH. HE CALLS ME UP AND ASKS ME

230
00:08:17,664 --> 00:08:19,540
IF HE CAN EDIT MY NEW MOVIE.

231
00:08:19,582 --> 00:08:21,084
CAN YOU BELIEVE THAT?

232
00:08:21,126 --> 00:08:23,503
YOU KNOW, I HAVEN'T
SPOKEN TO HIM

233
00:08:23,544 --> 00:08:27,048
IN WHAT, TEN YEARS, AND
HE ASKS ME FOR A FAVOR?

234
00:08:28,967 --> 00:08:32,429
YEAH, I'VE
ALWAYS HATED THAT HOWIE.

235
00:08:32,471 --> 00:08:34,514
NO, NO "HOW YOU DOING?"

236
00:08:34,555 --> 00:08:38,352
MAN, I MEAN, NOT EVEN
A CUP OF COFFEE FIRST.

237
00:08:38,393 --> 00:08:39,436
THE NERVE, HUH?

238
00:08:39,478 --> 00:08:40,479
YEAH.

239
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:43,523
REFILL?

240
00:08:43,564 --> 00:08:44,816
NOW THIS IS LAST MINUTE

241
00:08:44,858 --> 00:08:47,027
SO I WANT TO APOLOGIZE
FOR THE MESS, OKAY?

242
00:08:47,068 --> 00:08:48,111
WHO CARES?

243
00:08:51,323 --> 00:08:52,282
OH, MY GOD.

244
00:08:52,324 --> 00:08:54,201
SURE DIDN'T LOOK
THIS WAY

245
00:08:54,242 --> 00:08:55,702
WHEN I LIVED HERE.

246
00:08:55,743 --> 00:08:57,412
I KNOW!

247
00:08:57,454 --> 00:08:59,039
NOW, LOOK

248
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,165
THERE'S ONLY ONE PROBLEM.

249
00:09:00,207 --> 00:09:01,708
THERE'S ONLY ROOM FOR ONE

250
00:09:01,749 --> 00:09:03,543
SO I GUESS ONE OF YOU WILL
HAVE TO STAY AT JOEY'S.

251
00:09:03,584 --> 00:09:06,213
WELL, SINCE THE FIRE WAS
KIND OF MY FAULT

252
00:09:06,254 --> 00:09:08,548
I GUESS YOU SHOULD GET
TO STAY HERE.

253
00:09:08,589 --> 00:09:10,342
HEY, HEY, HEY,
NOW, THIS WAS

254
00:09:10,384 --> 00:09:12,386
NO ONE'S FAULT,
PHEEBS, OKAY?

255
00:09:12,427 --> 00:09:13,887
IT WAS AN ACCIDENT.

256
00:09:13,928 --> 00:09:15,805
IT WAS MY FAULT,
SO YOU SHOULD GET
THE NICE ROOM.

257
00:09:15,847 --> 00:09:16,848
OKAY!

258
00:09:16,890 --> 00:09:17,849
WOO-WOO!

259
00:09:17,891 --> 00:09:19,393
RACH, YOU'RE
THE FIRST GUEST

260
00:09:19,434 --> 00:09:20,852
AT HOTEL MONICA.

261
00:09:20,894 --> 00:09:21,853
HOTEL MONICA!

262
00:09:21,895 --> 00:09:22,979
JUST TELL ME HOW

263
00:09:23,021 --> 00:09:24,523
YOU LIKE YOUR EGGS
IN THE MORNING.

264
00:09:24,605 --> 00:09:26,774
I THOUGHT I WOULD BRING THEM
TO YOU, YOU KNOW, IN BED.

265
00:09:26,816 --> 00:09:28,360
WELL, YOU'VE BEEN
THROUGH SO MUCH.

266
00:09:28,402 --> 00:09:29,610
I HAVE.

267
00:09:31,112 --> 00:09:34,615
THIS RIGHT HERE IS
WHERE I KEEP THE PIZZA

268
00:09:34,657 --> 00:09:37,744
AND, UH, THAT'S WHERE
THE NAPKIN IS.

269
00:09:37,785 --> 00:09:39,954
WHAT'S THAT SMELL?

270
00:09:39,996 --> 00:09:41,956
I KNOW.

271
00:09:45,460 --> 00:09:46,420
OH, PLEASE.

272
00:09:46,461 --> 00:09:48,088
IT WAS SUCH A BIG CLASS.

273
00:09:48,129 --> 00:09:49,923
YOU NEVER
EVEN NOTICED ME.

274
00:09:49,964 --> 00:09:51,508
WHAT?
OF COURSE, I DID.

275
00:09:51,550 --> 00:09:54,553
YOU, UH, YOU SAT
NEXT TO SLEEPY SLEEPERSON.

276
00:09:54,593 --> 00:09:55,762
WHO?

277
00:09:55,803 --> 00:09:57,097
OH, UH, I HAD TROUBLE

278
00:09:57,138 --> 00:09:58,806
REMEMBERING
EVERYONE'S NAME

279
00:09:58,848 --> 00:10:01,101
SO I KIND OF CAME
UP WITH NICKNAMES.

280
00:10:01,142 --> 00:10:03,644
LIKE THE GUY ON THE OTHER
SIDE OF YOU WAS

281
00:10:03,686 --> 00:10:05,439
UH, SMELLY VON BROWN SHIRT.

282
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:07,148
OH, YEAH.

283
00:10:07,190 --> 00:10:10,444
SO, UH, DID YOU HAVE
A NICKNAME FOR ME?

284
00:10:10,485 --> 00:10:12,195
OH, NO, NO.

285
00:10:12,237 --> 00:10:13,321
YES, YOU DID.

286
00:10:13,363 --> 00:10:14,406
WHAT WAS IT?

287
00:10:14,448 --> 00:10:18,785
UM, IT'S CUTIE McPRETTY.

288
00:10:18,826 --> 00:10:23,582
OH, THAT'S SO SWEET.

289
00:10:23,622 --> 00:10:25,083
LISTEN, I GOT
TO TELL YOU

290
00:10:25,125 --> 00:10:26,501
I'M HAVING A GREAT TIME.

291
00:10:26,543 --> 00:10:28,128
YOU KNOW HOW
BEFORE YOU SAID

292
00:10:28,169 --> 00:10:29,212
IT MIGHT BE WEIRD

293
00:10:29,254 --> 00:10:30,964
THE WHOLE
STUDENT-TEACHER THING?

294
00:10:31,005 --> 00:10:32,215
AND TO BE FRANK

295
00:10:32,257 --> 00:10:34,468
I THOUGHT IT WOULD BE,
TOO, BUT IT'S NOT.

296
00:10:34,509 --> 00:10:36,010
I MEAN, IT'S NOT AT ALL.

297
00:10:40,181 --> 00:10:40,807
DR. GELLER!

298
00:10:40,848 --> 00:10:42,392
BURT!

299
00:10:45,145 --> 00:10:46,980
SO, DID YOU SLEEP
WELL LAST NIGHT?

300
00:10:47,021 --> 00:10:48,523
I DID.
YEAH?

301
00:10:48,565 --> 00:10:49,816
MONICA WAS SO SWEET.

302
00:10:49,857 --> 00:10:52,026
SHE LEFT A LITTLE MINT
ON MY PILLOW.

303
00:10:52,068 --> 00:10:53,694
YOU KNOW WHAT JOEY LEFT
ON MY PILLOW?

304
00:10:53,736 --> 00:10:54,862
WHAT?

305
00:10:54,904 --> 00:10:56,156
GUM.

306
00:10:56,197 --> 00:10:59,200
WELL, WE DETERMINED
THE CAUSE OF THE FIRE.

307
00:10:59,242 --> 00:11:00,535
YEAH, I KNOW, I KNOW.

308
00:11:00,577 --> 00:11:02,370
IT WAS MY CANDLE, MY CANDLE.

309
00:11:02,412 --> 00:11:05,206
NO. THERE WAS AN APPLIANCE
LEFT ON IN THE BATHROOM.

310
00:11:05,248 --> 00:11:06,874
IT LOOKS LIKE A CURLING IRON.

311
00:11:06,916 --> 00:11:08,168
I DON'T USE A CURLING IRON.

312
00:11:08,209 --> 00:11:09,544
WELL, SOMEONE DOES.

313
00:11:10,462 --> 00:11:12,046
DON'T LOOK AT ME.

314
00:11:12,088 --> 00:11:13,632
MY HAIR'S STRAIGHT.
STRAIGHT, STRAIGHT, STRAIGHT.

315
00:11:13,672 --> 00:11:16,050
COULD HAVE BEEN
A HAIR STRAIGHTENER.

316
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:19,053
OH.

317
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:21,973
THIS IS WHERE
I KEEP THE PIZZA

318
00:11:22,015 --> 00:11:25,226
AND... HEY, WHERE'D
THE NAPKIN GO?

319
00:11:32,108 --> 00:11:33,734
NOW, THERE YOU GO.

320
00:11:33,776 --> 00:11:36,154
I WOULDN'T WANT MY BEST GUEST
TO STRAIN HER EYES.

321
00:11:36,196 --> 00:11:38,239
THANKS, MONICA.

322
00:11:38,281 --> 00:11:39,824
DOES THAT SMELL
BOTHER YOU?

323
00:11:39,866 --> 00:11:40,992
THE SMELL FROM JOEY'S?

324
00:11:41,034 --> 00:11:43,203
NO. I CAN HARDLY SMELL
IT OVER HERE.

325
00:11:43,244 --> 00:11:44,496
OKAY.

326
00:11:44,538 --> 00:11:46,039
WELL, YOU LET ME KNOW
IF YOU CAN.

327
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:48,375
'CAUSE, YOU KNOW, I CAN BAKE
A PIE TO COVER IT.

328
00:11:48,416 --> 00:11:50,210
I CAN SMELL IT A LITTLE.

329
00:11:50,251 --> 00:11:51,252
BAKE THE PIE.

330
00:11:51,294 --> 00:11:52,420
OKAY.

331
00:11:52,462 --> 00:11:55,674
( phone ringing )

332
00:11:55,714 --> 00:11:57,800
HELLO.

333
00:11:57,842 --> 00:11:59,177
OH, YES.
ONE MINUTE, PLEASE.

334
00:11:59,219 --> 00:12:00,887
IT'S FOR YOU.
IT'S THE FIRE INSPECTOR.

335
00:12:00,928 --> 00:12:01,929
OH.

336
00:12:01,971 --> 00:12:02,930
HELLO.

337
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:04,932
YEAH, THIS IS PHOEBE.

338
00:12:04,974 --> 00:12:06,267
REALLY?

339
00:12:06,309 --> 00:12:08,186
( slightly disguising voice):
YEAH.

340
00:12:08,228 --> 00:12:09,354
SO, IT TURNS OUT

341
00:12:09,396 --> 00:12:11,105
THAT IT WASN'T THE HAIR
STRAIGHTENER

342
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:12,273
THAT STARTED THE FIRE.

343
00:12:12,315 --> 00:12:13,858
NO, NO.
IT WAS THE CANDLES.

344
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:15,109
YEAH.

345
00:12:15,151 --> 00:12:16,735
IT'S VERY NOT GOOD

346
00:12:16,777 --> 00:12:18,779
LEAVING CANDLES UNATTENDED.

347
00:12:18,821 --> 00:12:21,199
IN FACT, ONE OF
THE FIRST THINGS

348
00:12:21,241 --> 00:12:23,368
THEY TEACH YOU
IN FIRE SCHOOL

349
00:12:23,410 --> 00:12:24,911
IS, UH...

350
00:12:27,288 --> 00:12:28,289
UH, OKAY.

351
00:12:28,331 --> 00:12:29,874
WELL, I HAVE TO GO NOW.

352
00:12:34,837 --> 00:12:36,339
WE HAD SUCH A GREAT TIME.

353
00:12:36,381 --> 00:12:37,882
SHE'S INCREDIBLE.

354
00:12:37,924 --> 00:12:40,260
I THOUGHT THE AGE DIFFERENCE
MIGHT BE A PROBLEM

355
00:12:40,301 --> 00:12:41,386
BUT IT WASN'T.

356
00:12:41,428 --> 00:12:42,554
IT WASN'T AT ALL.

357
00:12:42,596 --> 00:12:44,431
ELIZABETH IS VERY MATURE
FOR HER AGE.

358
00:12:48,976 --> 00:12:52,105
A CONCEPT LOST
ON SOME PEOPLE.

359
00:12:52,146 --> 00:12:53,940
SO, IT'S OKAY TO
DATE A STUDENT?

360
00:12:53,981 --> 00:12:55,233
WELL, NOT REALLY.

361
00:12:55,275 --> 00:12:56,610
I MEAN, TECHNICALLY

362
00:12:56,651 --> 00:12:58,319
IT'S NOT AGAINST THE RULES
OR ANYTHING

363
00:12:58,361 --> 00:12:59,571
BUT IT IS FROWNED UPON.

364
00:12:59,613 --> 00:13:01,322
ESPECIALLY BY
THAT PROFESSOR

365
00:13:01,364 --> 00:13:02,823
WE RAN INTO LAST NIGHT--

366
00:13:02,865 --> 00:13:04,451
JUDGEY VON
HOLIER-THAN-THOU.

367
00:13:07,328 --> 00:13:08,955
WELL, ROSS, YOU JUST BE CAREFUL,
OKAY.

368
00:13:08,996 --> 00:13:10,457
YOU DON'T WANT TO GET
A REPUTATION

369
00:13:10,498 --> 00:13:12,500
AS, YOU KNOW, PROFESSOR
McNAILS-HIS-STUDENTS.

370
00:13:14,919 --> 00:13:16,212
YEAH.

371
00:13:16,254 --> 00:13:17,380
WHAT SHOULD I DO?

372
00:13:17,422 --> 00:13:19,006
WELL, ROSS, IT SEEMS
PRETTY CLEAR.

373
00:13:19,048 --> 00:13:20,174
WHAT'S
MORE IMPORTANT--

374
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:21,800
WHAT PEOPLE THINK
OR HOW YOU FEEL?

375
00:13:21,842 --> 00:13:24,304
ROSS, YOU GOT
TO FOLLOW YOUR HEART.

376
00:13:24,345 --> 00:13:26,013
JOEY, THAT IS SO SWEET.

377
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:31,519
HEY.

378
00:13:31,561 --> 00:13:33,688
HEY, HEY, SO,
HOW'D IT GO WITH DANA?

379
00:13:33,730 --> 00:13:36,274
ANY REASON I SHOULD LEAVE
A BLOCK OF TIME OPEN--

380
00:13:36,316 --> 00:13:37,609
SAY, THURSDAY?

381
00:13:37,651 --> 00:13:38,985
I COULDN'T DO IT.

382
00:13:39,026 --> 00:13:40,194
YOU COULDN'T DO IT?

383
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:41,529
RELAX. I JUST NEED
MORE TIME.

384
00:13:41,571 --> 00:13:42,863
WE'RE GOING TO
DINNER TONIGHT.

385
00:13:42,905 --> 00:13:44,949
WHAT? YOU'RE GOING OUT
WITH HER AGAIN?

386
00:13:44,991 --> 00:13:46,743
GOING OUT
WITH WHO?

387
00:13:46,785 --> 00:13:49,788
UH, DANA KEYSTONE
FROM COLLEGE.

388
00:13:49,828 --> 00:13:51,372
OH, YEAH.

389
00:13:51,414 --> 00:13:54,083
WASN'T SHE...?

390
00:13:54,125 --> 00:13:55,876
NO, THAT WAS DANA KAPLAN.

391
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:59,005
All:
OH, YEAH.

392
00:13:59,046 --> 00:14:00,381
JOEY, YOU DIDN'T
EVEN KNOW HER.

393
00:14:00,423 --> 00:14:01,716
AW, WHATEVER.

394
00:14:06,721 --> 00:14:08,348
GREAT STORY AGAIN.

395
00:14:08,389 --> 00:14:10,684
THE YARNS THAT
YOU WEAVE.

396
00:14:10,725 --> 00:14:12,477
WHOO-HOO.

397
00:14:12,519 --> 00:14:15,854
YOU KNOW, I SHOULD
GET GOING.

398
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:17,023
OH, NO, NO.

399
00:14:17,064 --> 00:14:19,108
STAY, STAY, BECAUSE
YOU SHOULD...

400
00:14:19,150 --> 00:14:20,234
YOU SHOULD STAY.

401
00:14:21,235 --> 00:14:22,903
WOW.

402
00:14:22,945 --> 00:14:24,364
OH, I AM

403
00:14:24,405 --> 00:14:26,032
REALLY FLATTERED

404
00:14:26,073 --> 00:14:30,662
BUT I JUST, I DON'T FEEL
THAT WAY ABOUT YOU.

405
00:14:30,704 --> 00:14:33,373
OH, NO, NO, NO.
THAT'S NOT... NO, NO, NO.

406
00:14:33,414 --> 00:14:34,708
I'M SORRY,
CHANDLER.

407
00:14:34,749 --> 00:14:37,251
YOU KNOW, YOU ARE
SUCH A SWEET GUY

408
00:14:37,293 --> 00:14:39,504
AND I DON'T WANT
TO HURT YOU.

409
00:14:39,546 --> 00:14:40,839
OH, I WISH THERE
WAS SOMETHING

410
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:42,882
I COULD DO TO MAKE YOU
FEEL BETTER.

411
00:14:42,923 --> 00:14:44,217
NO, NO...

412
00:14:44,258 --> 00:14:45,552
REALLY?

413
00:14:45,593 --> 00:14:47,053
OF COURSE.

414
00:14:47,094 --> 00:14:49,430
WELL, IT JUST
HURTS SO BAD.

415
00:14:49,472 --> 00:14:50,765
I, UH...

416
00:14:50,807 --> 00:14:52,058
OH, I'M SORRY.

417
00:14:52,099 --> 00:14:55,895
WELL, MAYBE THERE IS
ONE THING YOU CAN DO.

418
00:14:55,936 --> 00:14:57,856
WHAT? ANYTHING.
ANYTHING.

419
00:14:57,938 --> 00:14:59,357
WELL, I MEAN, THIS IS

420
00:14:59,399 --> 00:15:01,609
JUST OFF THE TOP
OF MY HEAD NOW.

421
00:15:01,651 --> 00:15:03,570
UM, BUT I HAVE
THIS FRIEND--

422
00:15:03,611 --> 00:15:05,238
UH, THIS ACTOR FRIEND--

423
00:15:05,279 --> 00:15:09,409
AND HE WOULD KILL ME IF HE
KNEW THAT I WAS DOING THIS.

424
00:15:09,450 --> 00:15:10,785
UM, BUT, UM...

425
00:15:10,827 --> 00:15:15,039
WOULD IT BE POSSIBLE
FOR HIM TO GET AN AUDITION

426
00:15:15,081 --> 00:15:16,290
FOR YOUR MOVIE

427
00:15:16,332 --> 00:15:17,792
SAY, ON THURSDAY?

428
00:15:17,834 --> 00:15:18,877
ABSOLUTELY.

429
00:15:18,918 --> 00:15:21,128
BUT YOU'D REALLY
FEEL BETTER

430
00:15:21,170 --> 00:15:24,674
ABOUT ME REJECTING YOU
IF YOUR ACTOR FRIEND

431
00:15:24,716 --> 00:15:26,885
CAN AUDITION FOR MY MOVIE?

432
00:15:26,925 --> 00:15:28,219
THE HEART WANTS
WHAT IT WANTS.

433
00:15:28,261 --> 00:15:29,303
I'LL SEE YOU LATER.

434
00:15:35,769 --> 00:15:39,021
HEY, HOW'S IT GOING?

435
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:42,275
WELL, NOT MUCH HAS CHANGED
IN THE LAST FIVE MINUTES.

436
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:43,276
YES, IT HAS.

437
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:44,861
I MADE COOKIES.

438
00:15:44,903 --> 00:15:47,822
I'M STILL FULL FROM
YOUR HOMEMADE POTATO CHIPS.

439
00:15:47,864 --> 00:15:50,199
BUT YOU SHOULD
EAT THEM NOW

440
00:15:50,241 --> 00:15:53,160
'CAUSE THEY'RE HOT
FROM THE OVEN.

441
00:15:53,202 --> 00:15:54,495
OKAY.

442
00:15:54,537 --> 00:15:55,830
OH, BUT NOT IN HERE.

443
00:15:55,872 --> 00:15:58,040
YOU CAN'T EAT THEM
IN BED, REMEMBER?

444
00:15:58,082 --> 00:15:59,250
NO CRUMBIES.

445
00:15:59,292 --> 00:16:00,501
OKAY.

446
00:16:00,543 --> 00:16:02,712
I'LL BE OUT IN A SECOND.

447
00:16:02,754 --> 00:16:04,589
OKAY.

448
00:16:12,054 --> 00:16:13,389
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

449
00:16:13,431 --> 00:16:15,224
THIS DOESN'T LOCK,
DOES IT?

450
00:16:19,771 --> 00:16:22,523
OH, JOEY, I'M SORRY.

451
00:16:22,565 --> 00:16:24,108
OH, THAT'S ALL RIGHT.

452
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:25,819
DON'T WORRY ABOUT IT.

453
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:26,945
NO. BUT LOOK.

454
00:16:26,986 --> 00:16:28,571
OH, THAT'S GOING
TO LEAVE A STAIN.

455
00:16:28,613 --> 00:16:29,697
RACH, HEY,
IT'S FINE.

456
00:16:29,739 --> 00:16:32,742
YOU'RE AT JOEY'S.

457
00:16:32,784 --> 00:16:33,868
REALLY?

458
00:16:33,910 --> 00:16:34,869
YEAH.

459
00:16:34,911 --> 00:16:35,912
LOOK.

460
00:16:41,041 --> 00:16:42,919
I'VE NEVER LIVED
LIKE THIS BEFORE.

461
00:16:42,961 --> 00:16:44,754
I KNOW.

462
00:16:48,174 --> 00:16:50,134
WELL, DON'T WASTE IT.
IT'S STILL FOOD.

463
00:16:50,176 --> 00:16:52,762
GEEZ.

464
00:16:57,391 --> 00:16:58,810
WHAT DO YOU WANT
TO DO NOW, HUH?

465
00:16:58,852 --> 00:17:00,060
YOU WANT TO GO GET
A DRINK?

466
00:17:00,102 --> 00:17:01,228
UH, I CAN'T.

467
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:02,229
YOU HAVE

468
00:17:02,271 --> 00:17:03,356
SOME STUDYING TO DO?

469
00:17:03,397 --> 00:17:06,233
NO, I HAVE SOME
TURNING 21 TO DO.

470
00:17:06,275 --> 00:17:07,652
OKAY.

471
00:17:07,694 --> 00:17:09,821
YOU KNOW, I REMEMBER
WHEN I WAS IN COLLEGE

472
00:17:09,863 --> 00:17:10,947
WE USED TO...

473
00:17:13,908 --> 00:17:15,242
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

474
00:17:15,284 --> 00:17:16,619
NOTHING.

475
00:17:16,661 --> 00:17:19,831
I'M JUST, I'M SO
COMFORTABLE WITH YOU.

476
00:17:21,958 --> 00:17:24,585
DO YOU NOT WANT
TO BE SEEN WITH ME?

477
00:17:24,627 --> 00:17:25,962
OF COURSE, I DO.

478
00:17:26,004 --> 00:17:27,213
ARE THEY GONE?

479
00:17:27,254 --> 00:17:29,089
UH, NO, THEY'RE STILL HERE

480
00:17:29,131 --> 00:17:31,258
BUT I THINK
I'M ABOUT TO LEAVE.

481
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,593
WHAT?

482
00:17:32,635 --> 00:17:34,012
NO, NO, WAIT.

483
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:35,053
YOU'RE RIGHT.

484
00:17:35,095 --> 00:17:36,096
THIS IS STUPID.

485
00:17:36,138 --> 00:17:38,098
WHO CARES WHAT
PEOPLE THINK?

486
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:40,601
I MEAN, WE LIKE
EACH OTHER, RIGHT?

487
00:17:40,643 --> 00:17:43,021
THERE'S NOTHING WRONG
WITH THAT.

488
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:44,605
COME ON.

489
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:48,526
BURT.

490
00:17:48,568 --> 00:17:50,570
LYDIA.

491
00:17:50,611 --> 00:17:51,905
MEL.

492
00:17:53,364 --> 00:17:54,490
THIS IS ELIZABETH.

493
00:17:54,532 --> 00:17:55,783
HI.

494
00:17:55,825 --> 00:17:57,869
AREN'T YOU IN MY
POPULAR CULTURE CLASS?

495
00:17:57,911 --> 00:17:59,453
Ross:
THAT'S RIGHT, LYDIA.

496
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:01,414
ELIZABETH HERE
IS A STUDENT

497
00:18:01,455 --> 00:18:03,123
AND, UH, WE'RE DATING.

498
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:05,084
AND YOU MAY
FROWN UPON THAT

499
00:18:05,125 --> 00:18:08,046
BUT WE'RE NOT GOING
TO HIDE IT ANYMORE.

500
00:18:09,422 --> 00:18:12,550
YOU ARE SO FIRED.

501
00:18:13,927 --> 00:18:15,094
WHAT?

502
00:18:15,135 --> 00:18:16,303
THEY'RE GOING TO FIRE YOU.

503
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:17,555
YOU CAN'T DATE A STUDENT.

504
00:18:17,597 --> 00:18:18,681
IT'S AGAINST THE RULES.

505
00:18:18,723 --> 00:18:19,807
REALLY?

506
00:18:19,849 --> 00:18:21,684
IT'S NOT JUST
FROWNED UPON?

507
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:28,983
I LOVE IT AT JOEY'S.

508
00:18:29,025 --> 00:18:30,860
HERE YOU GO.

509
00:18:32,445 --> 00:18:33,446
NICE.

510
00:18:33,487 --> 00:18:34,655
Rachel:
THANKS.

511
00:18:34,697 --> 00:18:35,698
SO, YOU BUSY THURSDAY?

512
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:36,783
OH, VERY FUNNY.

513
00:18:36,824 --> 00:18:38,325
I DON'T KNOW
IF YOU REMEMBER

514
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:40,870
BUT MY AUDITION WAS
SUPPOSED TO BE THURSDAY.

515
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:46,125
YOU GOT ME
THE AUDITION?

516
00:18:46,166 --> 00:18:47,460
LET'S HUG IT OUT!

517
00:18:47,501 --> 00:18:49,587
OKAY. OKAY.

518
00:18:49,629 --> 00:18:50,922
WHAT ARE YOU GOING
TO DO TO ME

519
00:18:50,964 --> 00:18:51,965
IF YOU GET THE PART?

520
00:18:53,257 --> 00:18:54,258
HEY.

521
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:55,301
HEY.

522
00:18:55,342 --> 00:18:56,636
LISTEN, UM...

523
00:18:56,677 --> 00:18:58,387
YEAH, OKAY, I NEED
TO TALK TO YOU.

524
00:18:58,429 --> 00:18:59,806
NOW, I KNOW THAT THEY SAID

525
00:18:59,847 --> 00:19:01,641
THAT THE, UM,
THE HAIR STRAIGHTENER

526
00:19:01,682 --> 00:19:02,767
STARTED THE FIRE

527
00:19:02,809 --> 00:19:04,310
BUT I THINK
I'M PARTLY AT FAULT.

528
00:19:04,351 --> 00:19:05,979
YOU SEE,
I DIDN'T TELL YOU

529
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:07,187
BUT, UM, BUT, UH...

530
00:19:07,229 --> 00:19:09,440
I HAD RECENTLY
REFILLED THE TISSUES.

531
00:19:09,482 --> 00:19:12,276
AND, SO, LET'S FACE IT,
THAT'S JUST KINDLING.

532
00:19:12,318 --> 00:19:14,278
SO, YOU KNOW,
I THINK IT'S BETTER

533
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:15,655
THAT I STAY AT JOEY'S.

534
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:16,739
NO, NO, NO, NO, NO.

535
00:19:16,781 --> 00:19:18,157
PHOEBE, THIS
WAS MY FAULT.

536
00:19:18,198 --> 00:19:20,493
AND BESIDES, YOU KNOW
WHAT, I'M FINE HERE.

537
00:19:20,534 --> 00:19:21,661
OKAY.

538
00:19:21,702 --> 00:19:23,287
CHANDLER, MONICA IS
LOOKING FOR YOU.

539
00:19:23,329 --> 00:19:24,831
REALLY?

540
00:19:24,872 --> 00:19:26,624
YEAH. SHE SAID SOMETHING
ABOUT CRUMBIES.

541
00:19:26,666 --> 00:19:28,208
NO, NO, NO.
I WAS SO CAREFUL.

542
00:19:30,586 --> 00:19:32,463
OKAY, YOU HAVE
TO SWITCH WITH ME.

543
00:19:32,505 --> 00:19:34,007
MONICA IS
DRIVING ME CRAZY.

544
00:19:34,048 --> 00:19:35,008
Joey:
THAT'S RIGHT.

545
00:19:35,049 --> 00:19:36,175
ALL THE LADIES

546
00:19:36,216 --> 00:19:38,218
WANT TO STAY AT JOEY'S.

547
00:19:39,261 --> 00:19:40,554
NO, NO.

548
00:19:40,596 --> 00:19:42,015
PHOEBE, I DON'T
WANT TO SWITCH.

549
00:19:42,056 --> 00:19:43,141
PLEASE, COME ON.

550
00:19:43,182 --> 00:19:44,642
I CAN THROW WET
PAPER TOWELS HERE.

551
00:19:44,684 --> 00:19:47,728
NO, BUT AT MONICA'S,
YOU CAN EAT COOKIES

552
00:19:47,770 --> 00:19:48,896
OVER THE SINK.

553
00:19:48,938 --> 00:19:50,397
I KNOW.

554
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:52,608
I'M SORRY.

555
00:19:52,650 --> 00:19:55,611
ALL RIGHT, FINE.

556
00:19:55,653 --> 00:19:57,196
THIS LOOKS LIKE
SO MUCH FUN.

557
00:19:57,237 --> 00:19:58,364
YEAH.

558
00:19:58,405 --> 00:20:00,574
GOD, WHAT A MESS.

559
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:10,084
WOW. IT ACTUALLY IS
IN THE HANDBOOK.

560
00:20:10,126 --> 00:20:15,131
I CAN'T DATE YOU OR HAVE
A HOT PLATE IN MY OFFICE.

561
00:20:15,173 --> 00:20:16,841
OH, I CAN'T BELIEVE

562
00:20:16,883 --> 00:20:19,844
WE HAVE TO STOP
SEEING EACH OTHER.

563
00:20:19,886 --> 00:20:21,387
FOR WHAT IT'S WORTH

564
00:20:21,428 --> 00:20:25,224
I DID APPRECIATE YOU
STANDING UP FOR ME.

565
00:20:25,265 --> 00:20:27,226
IT FELT REALLY NICE.

566
00:20:27,267 --> 00:20:29,854
KIND OF MADE ME
LIKE YOU EVEN MORE.

567
00:20:29,896 --> 00:20:30,980
I KNOW, I KNOW.

568
00:20:31,022 --> 00:20:32,815
I REALLY LIKE YOU, TOO.

569
00:20:32,857 --> 00:20:34,192
BUT WE CAN'T DATE.

570
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:35,818
IT'S AGAINST THE RULES.

571
00:20:35,860 --> 00:20:36,903
IT'S FORBIDDEN.

572
00:20:36,944 --> 00:20:39,321
WOW.

573
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:40,280
WHAT?

574
00:20:40,322 --> 00:20:41,615
JUST HEARING YOU

575
00:20:41,657 --> 00:20:43,701
DESCRIBE IT
AS FORBIDDEN--

576
00:20:43,743 --> 00:20:45,703
IT'S REALLY HOT.

577
00:20:47,914 --> 00:20:49,957
REALLY?

578
00:20:49,999 --> 00:20:51,918
YEAH.

579
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:55,504
WELL... I-I DON'T CARE
HOW HOT IT IS--

580
00:20:55,546 --> 00:20:57,506
IT'S.... IT'S WRONG.

581
00:20:58,591 --> 00:20:59,717
STOP IT.

582
00:20:59,759 --> 00:21:00,760
NO, NO.

583
00:21:00,801 --> 00:21:02,178
IT'S WRONG.

584
00:21:02,220 --> 00:21:05,431
IT'S-IT'S, IT'S NAUGHTY.

585
00:21:05,472 --> 00:21:07,474
IT'S...

586
00:21:07,516 --> 00:21:09,268
TABOO.

587
00:21:09,309 --> 00:21:10,811
SHUT THE BOOK.

588
00:21:13,773 --> 00:21:16,400
LET'S ALSO GET
A HOT PLATE.

589
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:24,784
SO?

590
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:26,535
SO...?

591
00:21:26,577 --> 00:21:27,787
IT'S THURSDAY.

592
00:21:27,828 --> 00:21:28,913
HOW WAS THE AUDITION?

593
00:21:28,955 --> 00:21:29,914
MONDAY, ONE DAY...

594
00:21:29,956 --> 00:21:31,040
TUESDAY, TWO DAY...

595
00:21:31,082 --> 00:21:32,041
WEDNESDAY...

596
00:21:32,083 --> 00:21:33,042
THURSDAY...

597
00:21:33,084 --> 00:21:34,210
( gasps )

598
00:21:34,252 --> 00:21:36,587
OH!

599
00:21:42,426 --> 00:21:46,472
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

